    "body": "Thanks, @jschuhmac! This already lgtm but I have one question about this choice:\r\n> The checks are only executed when the excitations were generated by a function (assuming that all other cases are handled elsewhere; ...)\r\n\r\nI assume you mean by \"all other cases are handled elsewhere\", that the default code from Qiskit Nature which get's triggered in common events handles everything properly. I agree that this is (hopefully :sweat_smile:) the case but does it hurt to run this check even in those cases? :thinking: \r\nThese checks should not be a real performance penalty here so I would argue to simply run them in all cases..",
